# Specialist Mechanic Finder ZA

A South African specialist automotive repair directory built with ASP.NET Core MVC, Razor, SQLite, EF Core, and a separate scraper console application.

## Overview

This project provides a searchable directory for South African auto repair businesses, with a focus on specialist workshops for specific vehicle makes and repair categories. It includes:

- ASP.NET Core MVC website with province/city filtering and specialist/general result sections.
- Shared domain model and ranking logic.
- SQLite-backed persistence using EF Core.
- Console scraper for importing CSV records and updating the same database.
- xUnit tests for ranking and database integrity checks.

## Prerequisites

- .NET 8 SDK
- SQLite (optional, local DB inspection)

## Solution structure

- `src/MechanicFinder.Core` – domain entities, DTOs, scoring logic
- `src/MechanicFinder.Infrastructure` – EF Core DbContext and SQLite seeding
- `src/MechanicFinder.Web` – MVC site and API endpoints
- `src/MechanicFinder.Scraper` – console ingestion and CSV import
- `tests/MechanicFinder.UnitTests` – unit tests for ranking rules
- `tests/MechanicFinder.IntegrationTests` – SQLite integration tests
- `data/` – CSV seed data and demo imports

## Build

```bash
dotnet restore
 dotnet build SpecialistMechanicFinder.sln
```

## Run the web app

```bash
dotnet run --project src/MechanicFinder.Web/MechanicFinder.Web.csproj
```

Open the local URL shown in the console, typically:

- `https://localhost:7156`

## Run the scraper

```bash
dotnet run --project src/MechanicFinder.Scraper/MechanicFinder.Scraper.csproj -- --import data/demo-businesses.csv --dry-run
```

## Database

The app uses SQLite and writes to `data/mechanicfinder.db` by default.

## Seed data

The application seeds:

- all nine South African provinces
- representative cities and towns
- sample vehicle makes
- sample specialty categories
- demonstration businesses clearly labelled as demo data only

## CSV template

```csv
BusinessName,Province,City,Address,Phone,Website,VehicleMakes,SpecialtyCategories,RatingSource,SourceUrl
Demo Volvo Specialist Cape Town,Western Cape,Cape Town,14 Main Road,0215550101,https://example.com/volvo-demo,Volvo,Automotive electrical systems,Google Maps,https://example.com/volvo-demo
```

## Notes on external integrations

- Google and Facebook are represented as extension points, not hard-coded dependencies.
- The app is designed to operate with local SQLite data even when remote APIs are unavailable.
- No live API credentials are included in configuration.

## How to adjust scoring

Ranking and confidence thresholds are maintained in:

- `src/MechanicFinder.Core/Scoring/SearchRankingService.cs`

This keeps the ranking logic separate from the MVC controllers.

## Limitations

- This is an MVP and intentionally demo-oriented.
- Optional remote integrations require credentials and can be layered in later without changing the search UX.
- Data added by the scraper should be treated as local or curated records unless verified through an authorised source.

